8</b> tuv</p></td><td><p><b>9</b> wxyz</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div><=
p>Return <strong>all possible letter combinations</strong> the input digits=
 could represent.</p><h4 id=3D"example">Example:</h4><pre><code class=3D"hl=
js language-python">Input: digits =3D <span class=3D"hljs-string">'69'</spa=
n>
Output: [<span class=3D"hljs-string">'mw'</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-strin=
g">'mx'</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">'my'</span>, <span class=3D"hlj=
s-string">'mz'</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">'nw'</span>, <span class=
=3D"hljs-string">'nx'</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">'ny'</span>, <spa=
n class=3D"hljs-string">'nz'</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">'ow'</span=
>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">'ox'</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">'oy=
'</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">'oz'</span>]
</code></pre></div>
<h2 id=3D"intuition">Intuition</h2>
<p>At each digit in the string, we have a decision to make: which letter wi=
ll this digit represent? Based on this decision, let's illustrate the state=
 space tree that represents the choices at each digit of the input string.<=
/p>
